  DriveEfficiencyChartWidgetUiTest, EnergyStatsWidgetUiTest, MileageStatsWidgetUiTest,
  PowerFlowHistoryWidgetUiTest, ProjectedRangeWidgetUiTest, SolarProductionWidgetUiTest,
  TirePressureHistoryWidgetUiTest). These files are committed and untouched by this artifact (git status
  confirms my footprint is only com/teslasync/feature-views/InfrastructureSection + the two test packages +
  this log). The repo's androidTest source set was already non-compiling, which is why the prompt gate runs
  the JVM testReleaseUnitTest, not connectedAndroidTest. The new InfrastructureSectionUiTest.kt is NOT among
  the compiler errors (the Kotlin frontend reports all unresolved references across the unit, so it is
  type-clean) and uses only resolvable APIs (assertIsDisplayed / assertCountEquals / onNodeWithText /
  onAllNodesWithText / performClick), the same ones the shipped WatchSummaryWidgetUiTest uses. Running the
  instrumented suite additionally needs a device/emulator (unavailable here). Fixing the 8 unrelated files
  is out of this artifact's allowed-files scope.

i18n: every string resolves through the Android resource facade (P1/S10) via resolveInfraText, reproducing
  react-i18next's natural-key fallback 1:1 with the web source. Catalog-backed keys (Mqtt, Migrations,
  Runtime, Topic, Message, Run, Success, Failed, Copy, Copied, common.offline) localize; the web's
  untranslated natural keys (Db Stats, Env Check, Send Test, the * Desc descriptions, No result yet,
  Request failed) fall back to the key text exactly as the web t() does. No hardcoded display literals.

States (faithful to the web useMutation source — NOT a useQuery surface): per-tool loading = run pending
  (Run/Send Test spinner); empty = idle (always-rendered "No result yet" result region, never a blank box);
  error = failed (Failed badge + error text: a verbatim 2xx {error} string, else a localized message);
  success = JSON payload + Success badge + copy. offline = connectivity-classified failure
  (Network/Timeout/CircuitOpen) -> Offline chip with the Run control still available to retry. "stale" +
  "auto-refresh" are query-only states with no analogue in this on-demand mutation source, so none is
  fabricated (honesty covenant: no red-as-green) — every state the web source actually renders is reproduced.

